  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) Sec. 2 (amends Constitution Sec. 145)\n(quote) No person who is not a citizen of the United States shall be allowed to vote in this state.[ but] The following persons also[are excepted and] shall not have the right to vote:[.]\n(section) Sec. 3 (amends Constitution Sec. 155)\n(quote) No person who is not a citizen of the United States shall be allowed to vote in said elections.\n(section) Sec. 1 (ballot question)\n(quote) Are you in favor of amending Sections 145 and 155 of the Constitution of Kentucky to prohibit persons who are not citizens of the United States from being allowed to vote in the Commonwealth of Kentucky, as stated below?\n(other) Sec. 1: sets the ballot question put to voters.\n(other) Sec. 4: the amendment goes to voters for ratification or rejection under Constitution Secs. 256-257 and KRS 118.415.\n(other) Sec. 5: Secretary of State must publish the question and amendment in a newspaper of general circulation no later than the first Tuesday in August before the election.\n(other) Sec. 6: Secretary of State certifies the question to county clerks, who place it on the ballots (dates differ for presidential and non-presidential years).\n(other) version: orig_bill: as introduced. Citizens-only voting language in slot e (Constitution Secs. 145 and 155); nothing in slots a-d.\n(other) version: 0007: the Acts Chapter 7 printing (enrolled act, 'Governor's signature not required'). Same words as orig_bill and bill, same slot e only.\n(other) version: bill: text as passed. Same words as orig_bill; only line breaks and header/footer codes differ. No committee substitute or floor amendment is recorded in the actions.\n(other) note: Same amendment text as HB 341 (the House companion). It is a proposed constitutional amendment; the saved text says it goes to voters at the next regular election at which General Assembly members are voted for. The files do not show the ballot result. Words struck from Sec. 145: 'but' and 'are excepted and'. The text ties the rule to voting, not to ID or proof of citizenship.\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
